1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,220
On a Graphs page, enter the function
you want to investigate and press Enter.

2
00:00:05,220 --> 00:00:10,020
Open Menu, choose Analyze Graph,
and select Minimum.

3
00:00:10,020 --> 00:00:13,510
We're looking for the lowest point
in the interval you choose.

4
00:00:13,510 --> 00:00:19,130
To set the lower bound, move the cursor
to the left of the minimum, then press Enter.

5
00:00:19,130 --> 00:00:23,960
For the upper bound, move to the right
of the minimum and press Enter again.

6
00:00:23,960 --> 00:00:26,670
Bracket just one turning point.

7
00:00:26,670 --> 00:00:30,330
The calculator marks the minimum
and shows its coordinates.

8
00:00:30,330 --> 00:00:33,220
The x-coordinate tells you where it occurs.

9
00:00:33,220 --> 00:00:35,780
The y-coordinate is the minimum value.
